Co-sleeping is a very endearing act of being able to share our dream and the bed of our bed with our son. We can give many details and benefits that are shared with this way of sleeping, although for some they may see it in the long run as a impairment in emotional growth of the boy or the girl.
4 Until when can you co-sleep?
Co-sleeping is the practice that parents have of sleep next to your son and sharing the same sleeping area. You can sleep in the same bed, but it is also called co-sleeping when the child is sleeping in co-sleeping cribs
The child shares the same sleeping area with the parents, and must be a clean, firm and safe place.
It is not advisable for parents to be under the influence of any substance or medication, or in a drunken state, as sleep can be unconsciously disturbed and cause an accident in bed.
Many parents support the co-sleeping and they have no qualms about defending it. no contraindications for it to be practiced and everything will depend on the limitations that a family with this practice wants and will want.
The baby feeling close feel safer sleep more peacefully and develop your neural system with better benefits.
On the other hand, it has been confirmed that it multiplies up to five times the chances that the baby do not have sudden infant death syndrome (SIDS). The Spanish Association of Pediatrics believes that it is a good and safe practice, especially when the baby is less than 5 months old.
What we can say is that it can recommend co-sleeping until one year of life of the baby. Before this age, if the child sleeps in another room, the increase in prolactin may no longer occur with the same guarantee.
