Once extracted manually or with a breast pump, we have to store it in its bags or containers.
2 How long does breast milk last in and out of the fridge?
If the milk has been expressed and is not going to be consumed immediately, it must be refrigerated so that it does not deteriorate. The ideal temperature would be between 4° or less, always in the coldest part of the fridge.
Once the breast milk has been extracted, either manually or with an electric breast pump, we must store it in specific containers. They may be BPA free glass jars or in special bags for the storage of breast milk.
preserved milk at room temperature (25° or less) has a duration between 4 to 6 hours maximum.
the stored milk in the refridgerator (between 4° or less) has a duration of 4 days. You have to look for a static cold place, inside a container that is not very contaminated and without any variation in temperature.
For a much longer-lasting preservation, you can always opt for freezing. The ideal temperature would be from -18° and it could be preserved from 6 to 12 months.
If this system is not available, it is better use the bain-marie, where the milk will be placed in a saucepan over hot water. In this way its heating will be very gradual and with the ideal temperature.
As a final note, it should be noted that once thawed milk can be usedat room temperature between 1 to 2 hours, if it has not been kept cold and has not been consumed has to be discarded.
Milk that has already been thawed cannot be refrozen, it would totally lose all its nutrients and texture.
