Even more: due to the 15 days that elapse between the last ovulation and the date of the last menstruation, from which the 40 weeks of pregnancy are counted, an overdue pregnancy is one that is delayed two weeks after the estimated due date. So you do have to act quickly to avoid risks to the mother or baby.
Addition estimated due date, there are several reasons why you can be in the 40th week of pregnancy and the baby is not born.
