How to teach your children to respect nature | Mothers Today
Maria Madroñal placeholder image | | Learning , Decoration , Crafts
Nature is the basis of our entire existence.That is why it is essential that we teach our children to respect it, since we cannot survive without water to drink, without plants to feed us and purify our air, without animals to feed us and accompany us, to really teach us things. important things in life.
2 Pollution, deforestation and liability
It is not necessary that we crush our children daily with this topic every day, but it is necessary that they know the consequences of our actions And know that if you leave a glass lying in the field, it can accidentally start a fire with disastrous consequences for the environment. It is important that they are educated with the knowledge that all our actions have an impact on nature.
It is also essential that they value the importance of water and not waste it or contaminate it, it is an irreplaceable resource for life. The springs, although they have remained there for centuries and even millennia, are not eternal if we dirty them or stop taking care of them.
Once they already know the negative consequences that their actions can have on the environment, it is equally important that positive reinforcement is exerted, showing the actions that positively influence the environment.They can be taught how much fun taking care of nature can be. For this there are multiple activities that can be carried out, which are an example for them.
We can also make countless crafts with recycled plastic bottles and jugs, including bags and CDs. It can be a very fun entertainment to spend a rainy afternoon and they will feel good knowing that they contribute to not generate harmful garbage that takes centuries to degrade.
Nature: mother of all families
