Hence, we are going to see why it occurs and what can be done to change it. First of all we shouldn't worry too much because we already know that children learn endless things and that they have their stages, so surely this will also be one of them and that it will soon end.
1 Why my son calls me by my name: Imitation
3 an act of rebellion
Why my son calls me by my name: Imitation
Another reason that your child may call you by your proper name is due to an emotional separation. That is to say, a kind of distancing that the little one notices.
an act of rebellion
Undoubtedly, in this case it is an act of rebellion, in most cases. So again we can say that it will be something that will not last long because they will go through another of the complicated stages in their lives.
Despite being transitory, it is best to take action on the matter and that everything returns to that normality that we like so much. Thus, when this happens and you hear your name you should not address him or her, as if it were not with you.
Jealousy between siblings is very normal, older siblings feel that their parents do not pay as much attention as before and the attention has shifted to the new member of the family. They need our attention and help to learn to manage this new situation in the best way.
3 How parents should react
-Wanting to be small again: they demonstrate this with evolutionary setbacks (they want to take a bottle, put on diapers, talk like a baby ...).
-It makes as if the brother does not exist: ignore it or treat it with indifference, as if it does not exist.
Pleasure joint activities: create activities that you can do with the two of you so that the older one does not feel left out: read them a story, bathe them together ...
Whenever you can give him quality time: he is still a child and needs the attention of his parents.
With patience and lots of love the situation will eventually normalize. If your child has aggressive behaviors with the baby, cut them in the bud, and if the situation gets out of hand, consult a professional.
As we all know, pregnancy is a time of constant changes in our body. The most frequent changes are usually hormonal, but there are still more that we will have to get used to, such as metabolic ones, even psychological ones, and of course, sleep disorders.
2 The best remedies to sleep better during pregnancy
Although the first weeks, as we had indicated before, we can feel more sleepy due to the increase in progesterone, this will change as the weeks go by. From there we will have to talk about the most common causes of insomnia in pregnancy.
Nausea: Sometimes they appear as soon as we get up and especially during the first weeks of pregnancy. But in other cases they last a little longer and appear in an almost unexpected way.
more frequent urination: Something also evident and that does not let us rest as we would like. Since the trips to the bathroom will be very frequent, because the bladder is more pressured and as such, we will no longer know what it is like to sleep in one go and a whole night.
Tiredness and fatigue: When we do not rest well at night and do not sleep the hours that correspond to us, the next day we say that we are not people. This results in great tiredness or fatigue.
We have already seen all the main causes of insomnia during pregnancy, well, now we are going to see some remedies to try to cope much better.
Meditation: It is another of the great ideas to be able to relax body and mind. In pregnancy we also need it and it will be favorable for our rest.
Similarly, don't eat heavy meals in the hours before you go to bed. Finally, remember to always go to bed relaxed, being able to do the sports and relaxation practices that we mentioned or, taking a warm bath.
The physical changes of the mother and the evolution of the fetus is very important, it is also important to take other aspects into account, such as the emotional changes that occur due to the whirlwind of hormones that a woman suffers during the nine months of the pregnancy.
During this trimester the baby will change from being a fertilized cell (a zygote) to being an embryo that implants itself in your uterine wall. It will grow to be like a peach and its body systems will begin to function.
A lot happens for you in the first trimester, too. Some of the more common early symptoms of pregnancy you may experience:
The second trimester of pregnancy begins in week 14 of pregnancy and lasts until the end of week 27. This trimester of pregnancy is for many women the most comfortable of the three, since for many women nausea and discomfort stop and go away.
During this trimester there will be some symptoms of pregnancy that still persist in you such as heartburn or constipation. In addition to the symptoms that you have already known up to this moment, there may be new ones because your belly does not stop growing, and that hormones also do not stop increasing.
Your baby is much larger than in the third trimester, he can weigh between two and four kilos (or more in some cases) at birth, he will measure between 48 and 55 cm at birth. The baby grows very quickly and this can also cause you to feel the painful kicks and discomfort in your gut.
When the pregnancy comes to term and your baby has been born, you will be able to meet the love of your life and you will realize how each week you have experienced during pregnancy, all the discomfort endured and the changes that you have been experiencing throughout the nine months of gestation, have been worth it.
