It is one of the widely used shelves, suitable for most warehouses or product goods.
Generally, the goods are stored on the shelf after being packaged by unit container equipment such as pallets and storage cages. The load of each unit is generally within 4000kg, and two units are usually placed on each floor.
The span of unit shelves is generally within 4m, the depth is within 1.5m, the shelves of low and high warehouses are generally within 12M, and the height of warehouse shelves is generally within 30m (such warehouses are basically automated warehouses, and the total height of shelves is composed of several sections of columns within 12m).
The height of each layer can be freely adjusted by an integral multiple of 75mm.
It has the characteristics of arbitrary picking of goods. Handling machinery such as forklift can reach any cargo location for storage, which is convenient and fast!
