Home > Our story > Join our team
We are a fraternity of people who care and, collectively and individually, help people change their trajectory for a better quality of life at every opportunity.
We are a strong purposeful team, focused on the big picture but we know the little things count. We are courageous.
If this sounds like you, then join us.
We offer a variety of housing types from short-term emergency accommodation through to transitional and long-term affordable rental housing across Victoria. We also provide specialist support services ranging from housing assistance for the elderly through to disability residential support.
The reasons to donate are all around us.
$20– prepaid phone card for a month
$100– Food and essentials for a family for a week
$500– Two weeks’ rent in advance to secure permanent housing options How to donate
The Australian Taxation Office has authorised Loddon Mallee Housing Services as a Deductible Gift Recipient, and therefore gifts of $2 more are tax deductible for the donor (some conditions apply).
We assist thousands of people each year who are in housing crisis, homelessness, or in financial stress, helping to address their complex and often compounding issues that have lead them to their current circumstances; whilst supporting their need to source appropriate housing options.
We are a not-for-profit company, with our roots established 40 years ago in Bendigo.
We are proud to be leaders in the community in speaking up and speaking out. Our team work consciously, collectively and collaboratively together to help the most vulnerable to become better versions of themselves.
Read some of our research and reports to find out more about the life-changing work we do and the social impact this has not just for our tenants, but the wider community as well. Learn more
We’re here for you.
Housing Support You will benefit from Housing Support if you need to get, or keep, a private rental property; have a low income and want to find affordable housing; or urgently need support finding somewhere to stay in the short term.
You will benefit from Case Coordination if you need support to get through a tough time. Your case coordinator will support you to come up with a plan, and will provide ongoing to support to make sure you have the best chance of achieving your goals.
Need another service?
Need to tell us something?
