Contractors play a vital role in protecting people from coronavirus because you attend several locations each day, and may come in contact with tenants at higher risk because they are elderly, unwell or experience disability.
Please find the necessary contractor documents from DHHS below.
PPE FOR Community service providers
Prior to accepting a job:
(A close contact is someone who has spent greater than 15 minutes face-to-face, cumulative, or has shared a closed space for more than two hours, cumulative, with a confirmed case of coronavirus)
If you answer ‘YES’ to any of the above you must not accept a job or attend a site, and you must contact Haven; Home, Safe immediately for further instructions. If the answer is NO, you should attend wearing Personal Protective Equipment as required including a mask, eye shield and gloves.
Before commencing works upon arrival and each day upon returning to the property, at a tenanted property, the contractor is to phone ahead and ask the tenant the questions below in regard to COVID-19.
(A close contact is someone who has spent greater than 15 minutes face-to-face, cumulative, or has shared a closed space for more than two hours, cumulative, with a confirmed case of coronavirus) Are you experiencing any of these symptoms: Fever, chills, cough, sore throat, shortness of breath?
On arrival at and each day upon returning to the property, the contractor must also check daily that their staff and any subcontractor working at the property answer ‘NO’ to all of the above questions. Before commencing work each day, the upgrade contractor must confirm with the tenant they have checked that their staff and subcontractors answer ‘NO’ to the above questions.
Wear safety goggles or face shield
The expectations of tenants, occupants and their visitors while the contractor undertakes the work are:
Work in common areas of properties
When working in common areas, contractors are at all times to:
The expectations of tenants, occupants and their visitors while the contractor undertakes work are:
Have you been identified as a close contact with anyone who has coronavirus?
for more than two hours, cumulative, with a confirmed case of coronavirus)
If the tenant, occupant or owner answers ‘YES’ to any of the above, they are to be advised the works must be placed on hold, and the contractor must contact Haven; Home, Safe immediately.
The contractor must also check daily that their staff and any subcontractor working at the property answer ‘NO’ to all of the above questions. Before commencing work each day, the contractor must confirm with the tenant, occupant or owner they have checked that their staff and subcontractors answer ‘NO’ to the above questions.
Practice social distancing (minimum 1.5m separation from others).
Wear a face covering (face mask supplied by the contractor if the tenant does not have their own)
If tenants, occupants, owners or their visitors do not adhere to the above requirements, the contractor is to request the they comply. If they do not then comply, the contactor is to leave the site immediately and report this behaviour to Active and Haven; Home, Safe.
Materials required may be left on site provided they are safely placed/stored.
It is essential that all staff are trained in the correct use of PPE – putting it on (donning) and removing (doffing), before it is used to ensure cross contamination does not occur. This includes use of face masks, gloves, protective eye wear, gowns or coveralls.
Face masks must be worn indoors and outdoors at all times. Face masks must be disposable surgical masks (P2 or N95 respirator/masks are
Put on the mask handling the side tapes or loops only:
If your mask has to be tied, tie the bottom first and then the top to secure on your face
After mask is in place never touch the front of your mask.
Undo the bottom tie of your mask first and then the top tie. Handling the mask only by the top ties, drop the mask straight into a general waste bin.
Masks can be used for up to 4 hours continuously but must be discarded if they become damp, dirty or damaged.
Hand hygiene should be performed when you feel that you may have contaminated your hands from touching
Both disposable and reusable goggles / face shields may be used.
If your eye protection is reusable, it must be cleaned and disinfected immediately after it is removed (for example with 70% alcohol wipes or a bleach-based disinfectant).
Do not engage in personal greetings, for example hugging, handshakes. Wearing a face mask provides an additional physical barrier to coronavirus (COVID-19), however face masks are not a substitute for physical distancing.
You are reminded that the health and safety of everyone on this site is a shared responsibility by all staff and contractors. Physical distancing is one of the key ways to control the risk of transmission of the COVID-19 virus.
