Every now and then I’ll talk to someone who says they want to become a Christian, but they seem to think the time isn’t quite right.
I never argue with them about their sins, but I do push back on their assumptions.
Being a sinner doesn’t keep us from Christ; it’s the reason we need Him.
In one of my favorite quotes, Charles Spurgeon urges us to stop looking to ourselves, and to start looking to Jesus.
‘I do not believe enough.’ That is looking to yourself.
‘I cannot discover,’ says another, ‘that I have any righteousness.’ It is quite right to say that you have not any righteousness; but it is quite wrong to look for any.
Righteousness isn’t what we need in order to come to Christ; it’s what we get when we come to Christ.
And when we put our faith in Him, we receive the reward for the perfect life Jesus lived.
It’s true that we’re not righteous enough, but the righteousness we need is found in Him.
We can’t just start our lives over, but the new life we need is found in Him.
So what are you waiting for?
