Reflection on the Conventions I watched most of the political conventions these last two weeks.
Every person on that stage tried to persuade you with personal stories and/or big promises.
Some of the talking points were straight up wrong too.
One of the things I realized was that while the parties were trying to sell you their candidates, they were also trying to sell you their worldviews.
In their view, the good life is getting wealthy when you work hard, and their candidate is the savior who can take you there.
And being rewarded for hard work is a good thing, but that can’t be where our hope lies.
Sin keeps us from God’s rest I pray this is an encouragement to you
