It’s normal to remember the day of somebody’s death.
It’s the end of a life, and it’s heartbreaking.
When important public figures die prematurely, we remember and mourn the day they were taken from us as well.
Yet, two thousand years ago Jesus of Nazareth was murdered by his own malicious assassins, and we remember that day as “Good" Friday.
The fact that wicked men would plot to murder the Son of God is tragic and it’s undoubtedly the greatest sin ever committed.
We can call that day “Good” Friday for many reasons.
