We decided on the “I’m Good” theme, we asked the Lord for help, and we started writing in opposite corners of Reach’s Atlanta studio.
Hopefully this explanation of the lyrics will help us to digest the content…
I hear the trouble’s coming for me, death is at my door way/
He said I ain’t guilty though I still ain’t had my court date/
We know that pain, trials, and maybe even death are imminent.
But that’s not what the Lord has told us.
I’ve tasted and I’ve seen Him, even though it’s just a foretaste/
But the goodness that I’ve tasted now is only a foretaste.
I don’t know what they feeling, I don’t know they thinking/
In this line, I was having a little fun with the Mario reference.
I can be wounded, I can be discouraged, I can even be killed.
When Super Mario gets that special blinking star, no matter what enemies he runs into, they can’t hurt Him.
You can rip my body to shreds, but my soul will remain intact.
They see me full of joy, like I don’t what He drinking/
People may see me fighting for joy in the midst of trial and be confused.
But I’ll get rewards from my Lord, it ain’t nothing better/
But I been purchased by my King, He’s forever with me/
But even if I never get another award or land on another chart, I’m good.
My records may not be purchased by anybody, but I’ve already been purchased and redeemed by Jesus.
No they can’t knock me down/
Once again, I don’t want folks to think I mean Christians don’t face trial, or even that we don’t feel the weight of those trials.
That’s why I’m making noise, that’s why I’m running hard/
All of the truth I mentioned above motivates me.
This is why I want to spit bars that catch people’s attention.
Here comes the pain, I’m good/
I’m just saying you can’t take us out the game, cause homie we good/
In the context of this song “good” doesn’t mean I’m perfect or righteous on my own.
“I’m good” is another way of saying, “I’m cool” or “Everything’s ok.” Because we’re in Christ, you can take everything from us, but we’re good because we’re anchored in Christ.
I know that I’ma suffer, that’ll only make me tougher/
These trials may even take my life, but believers don’t have to fear death.
The Lover of my soul’s with me, you can shake the brother/
Not guilty, He’s with us and He stays present/
These final six bars all testify to one anchoring truth, the Lord is with me.
There is absolutely nothing that can separate me from the love of God in Christ!
The most important thing about me is the fact that I’m united to Jesus.
Whatever comes my way, He has taught me to say, “It is well with my soul.”
