There are many people in our world today who think of themselves as spiritual or even religious people.
Maybe they even see Jesus as a great teacher or a prophet from God.
“So everyone who acknowledges me before men, I also will acknowledge before my father who is in Heaven, but whoever denies me before men, I will also deny before my Father who is in Heaven.”
So maybe we do confess that Jesus is Lord in our hearts.
Now, we have all been slow to admit our faith before others.
Christians are painted as morons who believe in stupid, harmful, and bigoted fairy tales.
But be warned, if we decide to deny Jesus before men, He will also deny us before the Father.
The proper response to the Christ is not shame or fear, but boldness and an eagerness to share Him before others.
You confess Jesus as Christ, and you are proud to say that you are a Christian.
In Titus 1, Paul speaks about false teachers denying God by their works.
Faith in Jesus will always change the way we live.
Our lust is a denial of God’s good plan for sexual desire.
All of our disobedience is a denial of God’s role as rightful Lord of all Creation.
If you do feel shame because of the ways you’ve denied Him, there is Good News.
