So, I was definitely in the minority at my high school (and by far in the locker-room).
You constantly hear negative comments from both sides about the other.
What’s tough is being ostracized by your own race for trying to reach out to the opposite race.
We are called to love our brother, no matter what skin color our brother happens to be.
But, the only way we will get there is by seeking to live out the gospel on a daily basis and being truly intentional about it.
