Whether it’s covertly bragging about who you know, or unashamedly pointing out all your accomplishments, bragging just isn’t cool.
Simply put, to brag is to “talk boastfully.” And all of us have been guilty of it at some point.
Bragging happens when you have something (or do something) so amazing that you think everyone needs to know about it.
If we’re honest with ourselves, we name drop and humble brag to our friends because we think it makes us look good.
The problem isn’t that what you’re bragging about isn’t great.
The problem is that the end goal isn’t so great.
Scripture speaks pretty strongly about this kind of boastful talk.
Those of us who’ve been redeemed by Jesus do have something to brag about – God Himself.
“Let not the wise man boast of his wisdom
that he understands and knows me,
justice and righteousness on earth,
Instead of using your words to acquire your own fame, use them to show off His.
The Earth was created to show His power.
Animals were crafted to point to His greatness.
You were built to brag on Him.
God bless you!!
